                        {
                            "id": "AID-D-001.002-G005",
                            "implementation": "Score media inputs against a trusted reconstruction-error baseline at API ingress and emit anomaly findings when inversion error exceeds the approved threshold.",
                            "howTo": "<h5>Boundary and verified inputs</h5><p>Use reconstruction error only when the deployment already has a signature-verified baseline for the exact model, inverter, generator, preprocessing graph, and media domain. The artifact-verification adapter must return the parsed baseline plus its verified digest; this module must not accept a caller-supplied “trusted” flag. A missing or mismatched artifact is an instrumentation error, never a clean image.</p><h5>Decode bounded media and score deterministically</h5><pre><code class=\"language-python\">from __future__ import annotations\n\n# File: detection/media_reconstruction_detector.py\n\nimport hashlib\nimport hmac\nimport io\nimport math\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport warnings\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Mapping\n\nimport torch\nfrom PIL import Image, UnidentifiedImageError\nfrom torchvision.transforms import functional as TF\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass VerifiedBaseline:\n    artifact_sha256: str\n    value: Mapping[str, object]\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ReconstructionPolicy:\n    policy_version: str\n    model_sha256: str\n    inverter_sha256: str\n    generator_sha256: str\n    preprocessing_sha256: str\n    media_domain: str\n    image_width: int\n    image_height: int\n    maximum_file_bytes: int\n    maximum_pixels: int\n    z_score_threshold: float\n\n\ndef _sha256(data: bytes) -&gt; str:\n    return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef _is_sha256(value: object) -&gt; bool:\n    return (\n        isinstance(value, str)\n        and re.fullmatch(r\"[0-9a-f]{64}\", value) is not None\n    )\n\n\ndef _finite_number(value: object, name: str) -&gt; float:\n    if isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n        raise ValueError(name + \" must be numeric\")\n    result = float(value)\n    if not math.isfinite(result):\n        raise ValueError(name + \" must be finite\")\n    return result\n\n\ndef _read_bounded_regular(path: Path, maximum_bytes: int) -&gt; bytes:\n    if (\n        isinstance(maximum_bytes, bool)\n        or not isinstance(maximum_bytes, int)\n        or maximum_bytes &lt; 1\n    ):\n        raise ValueError(\"signed media byte bound is invalid\")\n    if not hasattr(os, \"O_NOFOLLOW\"):\n        raise OSError(\"this reference reader requires O_NOFOLLOW support\")\n    descriptor = os.open(path, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW)\n    try:\n        info = os.fstat(descriptor)\n        if (\n            not stat.S_ISREG(info.st_mode)\n            or info.st_size &lt; 1\n            or info.st_size &gt; maximum_bytes\n        ):\n            raise ValueError(\"media is non-regular, empty, or outside the signed bound\")\n        data = bytearray()\n        while len(data) &lt;= maximum_bytes:\n            block = os.read(\n                descriptor, min(1024 * 1024, maximum_bytes + 1 - len(data))\n            )\n            if not block:\n                break\n            data.extend(block)\n    finally:\n        os.close(descriptor)\n    if not data or len(data) &gt; maximum_bytes:\n        raise ValueError(\"media changed size or exceeded the signed bound\")\n    return bytes(data)\n\n\ndef load_bounded_rgb(path: Path, *, expected_sha256: str, policy: ReconstructionPolicy) -&gt; tuple[torch.Tensor, str]:\n    integer_bounds = (\n        policy.image_width, policy.image_height,\n        policy.maximum_file_bytes, policy.maximum_pixels,\n    )\n    if (\n        not _is_sha256(expected_sha256)\n        or any(\n            isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, int) or value &lt; 1\n            for value in integer_bounds\n        )\n        or policy.image_width * policy.image_height &gt; policy.maximum_pixels\n    ):\n        raise ValueError(\"authenticated digest or signed image bounds are invalid\")\n    data = _read_bounded_regular(path, policy.maximum_file_bytes)\n    digest = _sha256(data)\n    if not hmac.compare_digest(digest, expected_sha256):\n        raise ValueError(\"media bytes differ from the authenticated ingress manifest\")\n    with warnings.catch_warnings():\n        warnings.simplefilter(\"error\", Image.DecompressionBombWarning)\n        try:\n            with Image.open(io.BytesIO(data)) as probe:\n                probe.verify()\n            with Image.open(io.BytesIO(data)) as decoded:\n                width, height = decoded.size\n                if width &lt; 1 or height &lt; 1 or width * height &gt; policy.maximum_pixels:\n                    raise ValueError(\"decoded image dimensions exceed the signed bound\")\n                rgb = decoded.convert(\"RGB\")\n                tensor = TF.to_tensor(TF.resize(rgb, [policy.image_height, policy.image_width], antialias=True))\n        except (UnidentifiedImageError, Image.DecompressionBombError) as error:\n            raise ValueError(\"unsupported or unsafe image\") from error\n    return tensor.unsqueeze(0), digest\n\n\ndef score_reconstruction(\n    *,\n    image: torch.Tensor,\n    image_sha256: str,\n    inverter,\n    generator,\n    baseline: VerifiedBaseline,\n    policy: ReconstructionPolicy,\n) -&gt; dict:\n    required = {\n        \"schema_version\", \"baseline_version\", \"model_sha256\", \"inverter_sha256\",\n        \"generator_sha256\", \"preprocessing_sha256\", \"media_domain\", \"mean_mse\", \"std_mse\",\n    }\n    value = dict(baseline.value)\n    if set(value) != required or value[\"schema_version\"] != \"aidefend.reconstruction_baseline.v1\":\n        raise ValueError(\"verified baseline schema mismatch\")\n    bindings = {\n        \"model_sha256\": policy.model_sha256,\n        \"inverter_sha256\": policy.inverter_sha256,\n        \"generator_sha256\": policy.generator_sha256,\n        \"preprocessing_sha256\": policy.preprocessing_sha256,\n        \"media_domain\": policy.media_domain,\n    }\n    if not isinstance(policy.media_domain, str) or not policy.media_domain.strip():\n        raise ValueError(\"signed media domain is absent\")\n    if any(value[name] != expected for name, expected in bindings.items()):\n        raise ValueError(\"baseline is bound to another runtime artifact\")\n    if image.shape != (1, 3, policy.image_height, policy.image_width) or not torch.isfinite(image).all():\n        raise ValueError(\"decoded tensor is incompatible with signed preprocessing policy\")\n\n    mean_mse = _finite_number(value[\"mean_mse\"], \"mean_mse\")\n    std_mse = _finite_number(value[\"std_mse\"], \"std_mse\")\n    threshold_z = _finite_number(policy.z_score_threshold, \"z_score_threshold\")\n    if mean_mse &lt; 0 or std_mse &lt; 0 or threshold_z &lt;= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"baseline distribution or signed threshold is invalid\")\n\n    with torch.inference_mode():\n        reconstruction = generator(inverter.project(image))\n    if reconstruction.shape != image.shape or not torch.isfinite(reconstruction).all():\n        raise ValueError(\"reconstruction is absent, non-finite, or shape-incompatible\")\n    mse = float(torch.mean((image - reconstruction) ** 2).item())\n    if not math.isfinite(mse):\n        raise ValueError(\"reconstruction score is non-finite\")\n    threshold = mean_mse + threshold_z * std_mse\n    if not math.isfinite(threshold):\n        raise ValueError(\"derived threshold is non-finite\")\n\n    return {\n        \"schema_version\": \"aidefend.reconstruction_finding.v1\",\n        \"control_status\": \"PASS\",\n        \"finding_status\": \"FINDING\" if mse &gt; threshold else \"NO_FINDING\",\n        \"image_sha256\": image_sha256,\n        \"model_sha256\": policy.model_sha256,\n        \"preprocessing_sha256\": policy.preprocessing_sha256,\n        \"media_domain\": policy.media_domain,\n        \"baseline_version\": value[\"baseline_version\"],\n        \"baseline_sha256\": baseline.artifact_sha256,\n        \"policy_version\": policy.policy_version,\n        \"mse\": round(mse, 8),\n        \"threshold\": round(threshold, 8),\n    }</code></pre><h5>Integration and verification</h5><p>The loader that constructs <code>VerifiedBaseline</code> must verify the baseline signature and digest against the deployment trust policy before calling this module; the model loader supplies the independently measured model, inverter, generator, and preprocessing digests. Replay valid, anomalous, malformed, symlink, oversized, decompression-bomb, wrong-binding, poisoned-baseline, NaN, and model-error fixtures. Read the emitted finding back by image digest and recompute its score with the same verified artifacts. Blocking remains in the applicable admission control; this guidance only emits a detector result.</p>",
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "AID-D-001.002-G006",
                            "implementation": "Cluster recent reconstruction-anomaly signals to identify coordinated bursts of suspicious synthetic media.",
                            "howTo": [
                              "<h5>Concept:</h5><p>A single anomalous image may be benign corruption, but a burst of similar high-error assets usually indicates a probing or deepfake campaign. This Detect-side control groups recent anomaly events so investigators can see campaign shape, not just isolated alerts.</p><h5>Step 1: Buffer recent anomaly events with stable features</h5><pre><code>from __future__ import annotations\n\n# File: detection/media_anomaly_burst.py\n\nimport hmac as _aidefend_policy_hmac\nimport json as _aidefend_policy_json\nimport math as _aidefend_policy_math\nimport os as _aidefend_policy_os\nimport re as _aidefend_policy_re\nimport subprocess as _aidefend_policy_subprocess\nimport tempfile as _aidefend_policy_tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path as _AidefendPolicyPath\n\n\ndef _aidefend_write_private(path, payload):\n    descriptor = _aidefend_policy_os.open(\n        path,\n        _aidefend_policy_os.O_WRONLY\n        | _aidefend_policy_os.O_CREAT\n        | _aidefend_policy_os.O_EXCL,\n        0o600,\n    )\n    with _aidefend_policy_os.fdopen(descriptor, \"wb\") as stream:\n        stream.write(payload)\n        stream.flush()\n        _aidefend_policy_os.fsync(stream.fileno())\n    _aidefend_policy_os.chmod(path, 0o400)\n\n\ndef _aidefend_strict_json(raw):\n    def reject_duplicate_keys(pairs):\n        value = {}\n        for key, item in pairs:\n            if key in value:\n                raise ValueError(\"duplicate JSON key: \" + key)\n            value[key] = item\n        return value\n\n    return _aidefend_policy_json.loads(\n        raw.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\"),\n        object_pairs_hook=reject_duplicate_keys,\n        parse_constant=lambda value: (_ for _ in ()).throw(\n            ValueError(\"non-finite JSON constant: \" + value)\n        ),\n    )\n\n\ndef _aidefend_load_signed_policy(*, path_env, signature_env, key_env, schema_version):\n    policy_path = _AidefendPolicyPath(_aidefend_policy_os.environ[path_env])\n    signature_path = _AidefendPolicyPath(_aidefend_policy_os.environ[signature_env])\n    if policy_path == signature_path:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"policy and signature paths must differ\")\n    policy_raw = policy_path.read_bytes()\n    signature_raw = signature_path.read_bytes()\n    key_reference = _aidefend_policy_os.environ[key_env]\n    remote_key = bool(_aidefend_policy_re.match(\n        r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9+.-]*:(?://)?\", key_reference\n    )) and not key_reference.startswith(\"-----BEGIN \")\n    key_raw = None if remote_key else (\n        key_reference.encode(\"utf-8\")\n        if key_reference.startswith(\"-----BEGIN \")\n        else _AidefendPolicyPath(key_reference).read_bytes()\n    )\n    verify_timeout = float(_aidefend_policy_os.environ[\"AIDEFEND_POLICY_VERIFY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS\"])\n    if not _aidefend_policy_math.isfinite(verify_timeout) or verify_timeout &lt;= 0:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"policy-verification timeout from the versioned runtime profile is invalid\")\n    with _aidefend_policy_tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(\n        prefix=\"aidefend-signed-policy-\"\n    ) as directory:\n        root = _AidefendPolicyPath(directory)\n        _aidefend_policy_os.chmod(root, 0o700)\n        policy_snapshot = root / \"policy.json\"\n        signature_snapshot = root / \"policy.sig\"\n        _aidefend_write_private(policy_snapshot, policy_raw)\n        _aidefend_write_private(signature_snapshot, signature_raw)\n        captured = [(policy_snapshot, policy_raw), (signature_snapshot, signature_raw)]\n        key_argument = key_reference\n        if key_raw is not None:\n            key_snapshot = root / \"verify-key.pub\"\n            _aidefend_write_private(key_snapshot, key_raw)\n            captured.append((key_snapshot, key_raw))\n            key_argument = str(key_snapshot)\n        try:\n            _aidefend_policy_subprocess.run(\n                [\n                    \"cosign\", \"verify-blob\", \"--key\", key_argument,\n                    \"--bundle\", str(signature_snapshot), str(policy_snapshot),\n                ],\n                check=True, capture_output=True, text=True, ",
                              "timeout=verify_timeout,\n            )\n            if any(\n                not _aidefend_policy_hmac.compare_digest(path.read_bytes(), expected)\n                for path, expected in captured\n            ):\n                raise RuntimeError(\"private signature-verification snapshot changed\")\n            policy = _aidefend_strict_json(policy_raw)\n        finally:\n            for path, _ in captured:\n                _aidefend_policy_os.chmod(path, 0o600)\n    if (\n        not isinstance(policy, dict)\n        or policy.get(\"schema_version\") != schema_version\n        or not isinstance(policy.get(\"policy_version\"), str)\n        or not policy[\"policy_version\"]\n    ):\n        raise RuntimeError(\"signature-verified policy schema or version is invalid\")\n    return policy\n\n\nfrom collections import deque\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nimport time\n\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.cluster import DBSCAN\n\nCORRELATION_POLICY = _aidefend_load_signed_policy(\n    path_env=\"D001002_CORRELATION_POLICY_PATH\",\n    signature_env=\"D001002_CORRELATION_POLICY_SIGNATURE\",\n    key_env=\"D001002_CORRELATION_POLICY_VERIFY_KEY\",\n    schema_version=\"aidefend.media-anomaly-correlation-policy.v1\",\n)\nWINDOW_SECONDS = CORRELATION_POLICY.get(\"window_seconds\")\nMINIMUM_EVENTS = CORRELATION_POLICY.get(\"minimum_events\")\nDBSCAN_EPSILON = CORRELATION_POLICY.get(\"dbscan_epsilon\")\nDBSCAN_MINIMUM_SAMPLES = CORRELATION_POLICY.get(\"dbscan_minimum_samples\")\nif (\n    any(isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, int) or value &lt; 1\n        for value in (WINDOW_SECONDS, MINIMUM_EVENTS, DBSCAN_MINIMUM_SAMPLES))\n    or isinstance(DBSCAN_EPSILON, bool)\n    or not isinstance(DBSCAN_EPSILON, (int, float))\n    or float(DBSCAN_EPSILON) &lt;= 0\n):\n    raise RuntimeError(\"signed media-correlation bounds are invalid\")\nEVENTS: deque = deque()\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass MediaAnomalyEvent:\n    ts: int\n    mse: float\n    face_score: float\n    embedding_distance: float\n    source_key: str\n\n\ndef add_event(event: MediaAnomalyEvent) -&gt; None:\n    EVENTS.append(event)\n    cutoff = int(time.time()) - WINDOW_SECONDS\n    while EVENTS and EVENTS[0].ts &lt; cutoff:\n        EVENTS.popleft()</code></pre><h5>Step 2: Cluster the recent anomaly stream and raise campaign findings</h5><pre><code># File: detection/media_anomaly_burst_query.py\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.cluster import DBSCAN\n\nfrom detection.media_anomaly_burst import (\n    DBSCAN_EPSILON,\n    DBSCAN_MINIMUM_SAMPLES,\n    EVENTS,\n    MINIMUM_EVENTS,\n)\n\ndef find_bursts() -&gt; list[dict[str, object]]:\n    if len(EVENTS) &lt; MINIMUM_EVENTS:\n        return []\n\n    feature_matrix = np.array([\n        [event.mse, event.face_score, event.embedding_distance]\n        for event in EVENTS\n    ])\n    labels = DBSCAN(eps=float(DBSCAN_EPSILON), min_samples=DBSCAN_MINIMUM_SAMPLES).fit(feature_matrix).labels_\n\n    findings = []\n    for label in sorted(set(labels)):\n        if label == -1:\n            continue\n        members = [event for event, member_label in zip(EVENTS, labels) if member_label == label]\n        findings.append({\n            'cluster_id': int(label),\n            'event_count': len(members),\n            'source_keys': sorted({event.source_key for event in members}),\n            'mean_mse': round(float(np.mean([event.mse for event in members])), 6),\n        })\n    return findings</code></pre><p><strong>Action:</strong> Feed reconstruction-error findings into a rolling burst-analysis job. Alert when DBSCAN or an equivalent density method identifies small, repeated clusters of anomalous media from the same source family or campaign window.</p><h5>Verify safely</h5><p>An independent verifier must replay the exact immutable event window with a separately pinned clustering implementation and compare membership, cluster labels, and burst findings, read the stored objects back, verify signatures and digests, and compare the canonical result digest.</p>",
                            ].join("")
                        }
