                    "id": "AID-D-008-G004",
                    "implementation": "Retrain and roll back only the D-008 fusion model from reviewed, evidence-bound D-008 outcomes.",
                    "howTo": "<h5>Concept</h5><p>Retrain only the D-008 fusion model from reviewed D-008 outcomes and source-finding evidence. Do not write labels back into D-002, D-003, D-011, or H-027 corpora from this workflow.</p><h5>Admit reviewed feedback</h5><pre><code class=\"language-python\">from __future__ import annotations\n\n# File: d008/admit_feedback.py\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\nREQUIRED = {\n    \"d008_finding_id\", \"feature_row_sha256\", \"source_evidence_sha256s\",\n    \"analyst_disposition\", \"reviewer_id\", \"reviewed_at\",\n}\n\n\ndef admit(record: dict, out_dir: Path) -&gt; Path:\n    if not isinstance(record, dict) or set(record) != REQUIRED:\n        raise ValueError(\"feedback schema mismatch\")\n    if record[\"analyst_disposition\"] not in {\"confirmed_malicious\", \"confirmed_benign\"}:\n        raise ValueError(\"feedback lacks a final reviewed disposition\")\n    evidence = record[\"source_evidence_sha256s\"]\n    if not isinstance(evidence, list) or not evidence or evidence != sorted(set(evidence)):\n        raise ValueError(\"source evidence digests are incomplete or duplicated\")\n    payload = (json.dumps(\n        record, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), allow_nan=False\n    ) + \"\\n\").encode(\"utf-8\")\n    digest = hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()\n    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    target = out_dir / f\"{digest}.json\"\n    with target.open(\"xb\") as handle:\n        handle.write(payload)\n    return target\n</code></pre><h5>Candidate cycle and rollback</h5><p>On the cadence or evidence trigger defined by signed organizational policy, build a candidate table from immutable admitted records, run the same training and independent promotion workflow above, and deploy by immutable digest. Keep the previous model and manifest available for rollback. A candidate that improves aggregate accuracy but breaches malicious-recall, benign false-positive, source-coverage, latency, or group-specific regression limits is <code>FAIL</code>. Missing reviewed labels or evaluation coverage is <code>INSUFFICIENT_DATA</code>.</p><p><strong>Action:</strong> Record the prior/candidate digests, admitted feedback population, H-007.004 evaluation manifest, promotion report, independent signature, rollout observation, and rollback result for every D-008 model change.</p><h5>Before you begin</h5><p>The fusion-model lifecycle owner applies this detector stage only when reviewed D-008 outcome evidence and a signed retraining policy authorize a candidate update; raw alerts or unreviewed feedback are never automatic labels.</p>"
