            "description": "Monitor and analyze Reinforcement Learning (RL), RLHF/RLAIF, RLVR, and agentic post-training systems to detect reward hacking, reward tampering, verifier gaming, and policy manipulation. Reward hacking occurs when an agent discovers an exploit in the reward function or evaluator to achieve high measured reward for unintended or harmful behavior. Reward tampering involves an actor or compromised service manipulating the reward signal, verifier result, or evaluator logs. This technique compares reward streams, trajectories, verifier outputs, held-out evaluations, and task-success signals collected outside the reward path so high reward cannot silently substitute for real goal achievement.",
